1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,480
At two minutes past six on a Thursday,

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,355
the whole world stops.

3
00:00:05,375 --> 00:00:06,800
Except you.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:08,665
You can wake one person.

5
00:00:08,685 --> 00:00:09,810
Just one.

6
00:00:09,835 --> 00:00:11,980
Touch their shoulder, and they're back.

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,456
You get one hour.

8
00:00:13,476 --> 00:00:15,406
Then the world carries on, and only

9
00:00:15,426 --> 00:00:17,550
that person will remember any of it.

10
00:00:18,139 --> 00:00:19,418
Who do you wake?

11
00:00:22,468 --> 00:00:24,098
The first thing you learn is that you

12
00:00:24,118 --> 00:00:25,868
can't move anything.

13
00:00:25,888 --> 00:00:28,318
A pigeon in the air is as solid as a

14
00:00:28,338 --> 00:00:29,383
wall.

15
00:00:29,403 --> 00:00:31,194
The second thing you learn is that a

16
00:00:31,214 --> 00:00:33,962
frozen city is very, very quiet.

17
00:00:34,952 --> 00:00:36,457
You eat a free sample.

18
00:00:36,477 --> 00:00:37,957
Then all of them.

19
00:00:37,977 --> 00:00:39,907
Nobody can stop you, and that turns

20
00:00:39,927 --> 00:00:41,931
out to be less fun than you'd think.

21
00:00:41,951 --> 00:00:42,885
Hello?

22
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:45,235
Fifty-two minutes.

23
00:00:46,225 --> 00:00:48,530
You find your boss frozen mid-sneeze

24
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,155
through the office window.

25
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:52,180
You look at it for a full minute.

26
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,111
It's the best minute of your week.

27
00:00:54,201 --> 00:00:56,731
A little boy outside the shop is frozen

28
00:00:56,751 --> 00:00:59,431
with an ice cream tipping off its cone.

29
00:00:59,451 --> 00:01:00,756
You can't fix it.

30
00:01:00,776 --> 00:01:02,506
You can't move anything.

31
00:01:02,526 --> 00:01:04,381
You just stand there and feel sorry

32
00:01:04,401 --> 00:01:05,777
about the ice cream.

33
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:09,022
The obvious choice is Mira.

34
00:01:09,042 --> 00:01:11,522
But Mira is four hours away by train,

35
00:01:11,542 --> 00:01:13,252
and nothing is running.

36
00:01:13,272 --> 00:01:15,542
On foot, she's three days.

37
00:01:15,562 --> 00:01:17,492
Mum is an hour's walk.

38
00:01:17,512 --> 00:01:19,442
You'd get there just as the world starts

39
00:01:19,462 --> 00:01:20,482
again.

40
00:01:20,502 --> 00:01:22,813
Theo is twenty minutes away, frozen

41
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:25,630
on the sofa with a controller, mid-scream.

42
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:27,350
He would be annoying about it.

43
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:29,305
He'd want to steal things.

44
00:01:29,325 --> 00:01:31,000
He would definitely want to draw on

45
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:32,070
the boss.

46
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:33,620
But he'd be someone.

47
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,720
In a silent city, someone feels like

48
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:36,549
a lot.

49
00:01:36,569 --> 00:01:37,909
Theo it is.

50
00:01:38,059 --> 00:01:39,789
You'd have a whole half hour of someone

51
00:01:39,809 --> 00:01:40,864
to talk to.

52
00:01:40,884 --> 00:01:42,492
You start walking home.

53
00:01:44,142 --> 00:01:45,437
Then you see her.

54
00:01:45,457 --> 00:01:47,537
A woman in a red coat, stepping off

55
00:01:47,557 --> 00:01:49,976
the kerb, looking at her phone.

56
00:01:50,001 --> 00:01:52,256
And a cyclist, frozen a hand's width

57
00:01:52,276 --> 00:01:53,831
away, looking at his.

58
00:01:54,522 --> 00:01:55,727
You can't move her.

59
00:01:55,747 --> 00:01:57,327
You can't move the bike.

60
00:01:57,347 --> 00:01:59,595
When the world starts again, they meet.

61
00:02:00,585 --> 00:02:02,704
You stand there for a long time.

62
00:02:02,724 --> 00:02:05,329
If you wake her, you walk home alone.

63
00:02:05,349 --> 00:02:07,788
Nobody will ever know there was an hour.

64
00:02:08,379 --> 00:02:09,229
If you don't, you'll know.

65
00:02:09,249 --> 00:02:11,833
For the rest of your life, you'll know.

66
00:02:12,743 --> 00:02:13,893
Oh my goodness.

67
00:02:13,923 --> 00:02:15,342
Why is it so quiet?

68
00:02:15,362 --> 00:02:16,392
Long story.

69
00:02:16,412 --> 00:02:18,349
Can you take one step back for me?

70
00:02:18,369 --> 00:02:19,594
Why would I Oh.

71
00:02:19,624 --> 00:02:20,387
Oh.

72
00:02:21,317 --> 00:02:22,900
That was going to hurt.

73
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:23,560
Yeah.

74
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,903
Is it just us?

75
00:02:24,923 --> 00:02:25,748
Just us.

76
00:02:25,768 --> 00:02:27,298
For about half an hour.

77
00:02:27,318 --> 00:02:27,868
Right.

78
00:02:27,888 --> 00:02:28,388
Well.

79
00:02:28,428 --> 00:02:29,433
I'm Rosa.

80
00:02:29,453 --> 00:02:31,071
I'm going to need to sit down.

81
00:02:33,021 --> 00:02:34,776
You have eight minutes left.

82
00:02:34,796 --> 00:02:37,185
You spend them on a bench with a stranger.

83
00:02:37,205 --> 00:02:39,275
Of everyone in the world, you woke me?

84
00:02:39,295 --> 00:02:40,748
You were the one who needed it.

85
00:02:40,768 --> 00:02:42,500
Who were you going to wake?

86
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,325
My brother.

87
00:02:43,345 --> 00:02:44,814
He'd have been annoying about it.

88
00:02:44,834 --> 00:02:46,854
Then I'll be annoying about it for him.

89
00:02:46,874 --> 00:02:47,549
Thank you.

90
00:02:47,589 --> 00:02:47,969
Thank you.

91
00:02:47,989 --> 00:02:48,578
Thank you.

92
00:02:48,598 --> 00:02:49,711
You can stop.

93
00:02:49,731 --> 00:02:51,861
I'm going to tell everyone about this.

94
00:02:51,881 --> 00:02:53,508
Nobody is going to believe me.

95
00:02:53,528 --> 00:02:54,734
Probably not.

96
00:02:54,754 --> 00:02:55,654
I don't care.

97
00:02:55,694 --> 00:02:56,693
I'll know.

98
00:02:57,743 --> 00:02:58,753
Three seconds.

99
00:02:58,773 --> 00:03:00,261
She squeezes your hand.

100
00:03:01,251 --> 00:03:02,731
The world starts again.

101
00:03:02,751 --> 00:03:05,214
The cyclist rides past nobody.

102
00:03:06,124 --> 00:03:06,854
Where've you been?

103
00:03:06,874 --> 00:03:07,899
You look weird.

104
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:09,459
I had a quiet hour.

105
00:03:09,479 --> 00:03:10,282
Lucky.

106
00:03:10,432 --> 00:03:12,462
Nobody else will ever know.

107
00:03:12,482 --> 00:03:14,662
One woman in a red coat will remember

108
00:03:14,682 --> 00:03:15,562
it forever.

109
00:03:17,952 --> 00:03:19,334
Who would you wake?
